Origin and attribution

This baseline was extracted from a private system in which the same lifecycle
grew alongside the application it was built to protect. What transferred is the
role model and the mechanics; the topology did not, deliberately and by design.
Nothing in this repository describes that system's network, hosts or addresses,
and no example here is derived from a real one.

Read that as the intended limit of the attribution: the value being shared is
the reasoning about which separations carry a security property, not a
description of somebody's infrastructure.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note on the warranty disclaimer

The disclaimer above is not boilerplate to skim past. This repository documents
security properties AND the precise points at which each of them stops holding
-- see docs/layers.md, where every layer states what it does not give you.
Adopting a layer without reading its limits is how a baseline becomes a false
sense of security, which is worse than no baseline at all.
